## AC1: FAIL, and that is the honest and anticipated reading
expect (?m)^CYCLE=\S+ STOPPED=\S+ FAILED=([1-9]\d*) NAMED=\1$
The regex requires FAILED >= 1 and NAMED == FAILED. This record holds NO failure, so there is no
detail for anything to name. AC1 cannot pass on it and nothing was done to make it pass.
CONTROLS on the regex itself, so the FAIL is the record's and not the pattern's:
  'CYCLE=X STOPPED=none FAILED=8 NAMED=8' -> MATCHES      (it can pass)
  'CYCLE=X STOPPED=none FAILED=8 NAMED=0' -> no match     (it really tests NAMED == FAILED)

